#: manual/api/binary_checked.md:119
#: manual/api/interval_checked.md:184
msgid "Composition"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/binary_checked.md:123
msgid "`map(f)` applies an infallible function to a success and leaves an error unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/binary_checked.md:130
msgid "$\\texttt{map}(\\texttt{Ok}(x), f) = \\texttt{Ok}(f(x))$ and $\\texttt{map}(\\texttt{Err}(e), f) = \\texttt{Err}(e)$; `f` is not called on an error. `map` can never turn a success into an error."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/binary_checked.md:136
msgid "`bind(f)` applies a function that may itself fail."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/binary_checked.md:142
msgid "$\\texttt{bind}(\\texttt{Ok}(x), f) = f(x)$ and $\\texttt{bind}(\\texttt{Err}(e), f) = \\texttt{Err}(e)$. With `ok` it satisfies the monad laws (left and right identity, associativity), derived in the [design page](../design/binary_checked.md#the-monad-laws)."
