#: manual/api/decimal_gda.md:1371
msgid "`compare_total` returns $-1$, $0$ or $1$ in the GDA total order. The order is by sign bit first. For positive values it is $\\text{finite} < \\infty < \\text{sNaN} < \\text{NaN}$, with finite values ordered by value and then by exponent (`2.50` < `2.5`) and NaNs by payload; for negative values it is reversed. `compare_total_magnitude` applies the total order to the absolute values: it is `compare_total` of the two absolute values (GDA 1.70, page 43), so in a subset context the sign goes before the operands are rounded ([#763](https://github.com/Luna-Flow/floating/issues/763)). The total orders never raise flags in an extended context."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/decimal_gda.md:1381
msgid "A subset context (`extended=false`) first rounds the operands to the precision, as it does for every operand (see [`GdaContext::new`](#gdacontextnew-gdacontexttry_new); GDA 1.70, page 56 (Appendix A, The X3.274 subset)), which raises `Rounded` and `LostDigits`. The [`Decimal` methods of the same names](#decimalcompare_total-decimalcompare_total_magnitude) compare the operands as they are."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/decimal_gda.md:1389
