#: manual/api/decimal_gda.md:1574
msgid "[`GdaContext::new`](#gdacontextnew-gdacontexttry_new) cannot build the working exponent range. It limits $E_{\\max}$ of a context to at most $999{,}999{,}999$ and $E_{\\min}$ to at least $-999{,}999{,}999$ (GDA 1.70, page 10 (Abstract representation of numbers) allows a limit Elimit without giving a value), and the working range fills the `Int` range: the largest adjusted exponent is $2^{31}-2 = 2{,}147{,}483{,}646$ and the smallest exponent is $E_{\\mathrm{tiny}} = -2^{31}+3 = -2{,}147{,}483{,}645$ for every $P$, so $E_{\\mathrm{tiny}}$ is always a valid `Int` exponent. A result above the range is a signed infinity (`1E+1500000000 * 1E+1500000000` is `inf`); one below it is rounded with the half-even rounding algorithm to $E_{\\mathrm{tiny}}$, possibly to a signed zero."
