"otin \\boldsymbol{b}$, the first output is the decorated quotient $\\boldsymbol{c} / \\boldsymbol{b}$ (the same decoration as `/`) and the second is Empty with `Trv`. Every other output, empty or not, is decorated `Trv`. `mul_rev` is a reverse-mode operation and has the trivial decorated version of 11.7.1: NaI if any input is NaI, else the bare result decorated `Trv`."
