#: manual/api/interval_checked.md:367
msgid "The context is `ArithmeticContext::new(x.precision())`; `interval` uses only its precision, and re-rounds the base and the result outward with `with_precision`, which adds nothing when they are already representable. `pown` encloses $\\{t^{n}\\}$ with `Interval::pown`, which treats the base as one point (so `pown(2)` of $[-1, 1]$ is $[0, 1]$, tighter than `x * x`, which is $[-1, 1]$). A zero base with a negative exponent gives the empty set. An empty base stays empty for every exponent, including `pown(0)`. There is no `pow_nat` here: a non-negative exponent is a `pown`, and the trait form `Interval::pow_nat_checked` takes a `UInt`."
