#: manual/api/interval_checked.md:468
msgid "These methods enclose the image of the interval under the hyperbolic functions and their inverses."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/interval_checked.md:480
msgid "Each method is `bind` of `Interval::try_<name>` at the interval's precision. The result $Y$ satisfies $f(X \\cap \\operatorname{dom} f) \\subseteq Y$; parts of $X$ outside the domain are ignored, so $\\ln([-1, 1]) = [-\\infty, 0]$ and $\\ln([-2, -2])$ is empty. The only error is a `CertificationFailure` when an enclosure cannot be certified, for example the cosine of $2^{8000000}$ (reason `ResourceLimit`). There are no context variants; precision is set with `with_precision`."
