msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/decimal.md:5
msgid "`decimal` is the IEEE 754 arithmetic and interchange surface. General Decimal Arithmetic sticky status and traps belong to `decimal_gda`; passing the GDA corpus does not by itself establish the IEEE claim."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/decimal.md:7
msgid "Independent IEEE corpus"
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/decimal.md:9
msgid "The committed IEEE corpus covers decimal32/64/128 DPD and BID interchange, canonical and non-canonical encodings, special values, flags, total order, and core arithmetic. The DPD fixture exhaustively checks all 1,024 declets."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/decimal.md:11
msgid "Oracle layers"
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/decimal.md:13
msgid "Mandatory operation vectors use exact integer/rational construction and the documented DPD/BID bridge. Elementary families use independent high-precision or interval oracles when available. Values or encoded bits and IEEE flags are recorded independently so a numerically plausible result cannot hide a flag error."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/decimal.md:15
msgid "The committed elementary layer contains 3,060 certified rows. MPFR 4.2.2 produces directed 768-bit dyadic endpoints; exact integer conversion rounds both endpoints into decimal32/64/128 under each of the five `DecimalRoundingMode` values, and the generator rejects a row unless result and flags are unique. Native, Wasm, Wasm-GC, and JavaScript each pass 573/573 public API tests after these rows are materialized (one test per MPFR interval, holding its 15 rows: a Wasm test module cannot register one test per row). The full gate, `just gate decimal 3`, is 64,327/64,327: the 23,031 target-independent checks, the 573 public API tests on each of the four targets, and the 9,691 rows of the `pi_inverse` table and the 60 rows of the `huge_trig` table on each of the four targets. RDFP and Arb remain optional secondary routes and are not counted when unavailable."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/decimal.md:28
msgid "IEEE 754-2019 §9.2 saturation regressions for `Decimal::tanh_ctx` and `Decimal::expm1_ctx` are in `library/src/decimal/elementary_extensions_wbtest.mbt`. They check positive and negative `tanh`, negative `expm1`, all eight rounding algorithms (the five directions of `DecimalRoundingMode` and three working ones), and the exact `Inexact` flag. The certified pre-loop bound selects a same-side representative within the proved gap and passes it through the normal context finalizer, which supplies tininess and overflow flags. These targeted cases are separate from the committed MPFR row count. `decimal_gda` currently exposes neither operation, so this entry makes no GDA conformance claim."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/decimal.md:41
msgid "IEEE Std 754-2019 for `decimal` (decimal32/64/128 and arbitrary precision). Status is `conforming` when the operation exists and the cited evidence exercises it, `partial` when part of the clause is missing or evidence is thin (the cell says which), `not implemented` and `not applicable` otherwise. `Level` is `required` for clauses the standard states with \"shall\", `recommended` for those it states with \"should\" (and for the optional parts), `optional` for features a flavor may leave out. Evidence without a corpus name is a unit test in the repository; \"no external corpus\" marks operations that no independent oracle checks."
msgstr ""

