#: manual/design/bench/external.md:259
msgid "What the method does differently on a runtime that compiles while it runs:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/bench/external.md:261
msgid "**Warm-up.** The code of a case may still be compiled during the first blocks. The warm-up time is a number of the method, fixed per runtime before any cell is measured, from the calibration experiment below. A flag `w` is reported when the median net of the first third of the pairs of every round differs from that of the last third by more than 5% of the net; it removes no data."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/bench/external.md:267
msgid "**The floor differs per runtime** and is measured in every pair, so the net handles it. A call site of the null's closure can be inlined where that of the case cannot, which makes the null cheaper than the harness part of the case and the net slightly larger; it errs against the library, and nothing corrects it."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/bench/external.md:271
msgid "**Calibration** of the batch size follows the warm-up, so it is done on warm code."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/bench/external.md:273
msgid "The calibration experiment of the warm-up"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/bench/external.md:275
msgid "Fixed here before it is run. One experiment per runtime (`wasm`, `js`), in the bench window of the measurement, with `just bench external warmup --target T`:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/bench/external.md:278
msgid "Cases: `binary/add/53`, `binary/mul/512`, `binary/ln/2048` and `decimal_gda/add/34` (a fast case, a mid-size case, an elementary function and a decimal case; the same operand file as the measurement)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/bench/external.md:281
msgid "Warm-up times: 5, 50, 200, 1000 and 3000 ms. Each (warm-up, case) is run three times, each in its own process, with no exploratory blocks and 60 confirmatory pairs, the standard calibration target of 20 ms per block."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/bench/external.md:284
msgid "Statistic of a run: the warm-up drift `w` of the design above, the difference of the median net of the first and of the last third of the 60 pairs, in percent of the net."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/bench/external.md:287
msgid "Rule: the smallest warm-up for which every run (every case and every repeat) has a drift of at most 2%; the warm-up of the runtime is twice that value, rounded up to a whole 100 ms. If no warm-up reaches 2%, the experiment is reported and the runtime is measured only with the `w` flag on and the longest warm-up, with the result stated as not resolved by the method."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/bench/external.md:292
msgid "The value, the table of drifts and the versions of the runtime are published with the first summary of the runtime and written into the `protocol` block of every later one. The native value is the preset's 5 ms and is not part of the experiment."
