#: manual/performance/binary.md:256
msgid "The certified `exp` enclosure bounds the Taylor series of the reduced argument (at most 1/8) in fixed point with 16 fractional bits beyond the working precision when the argument is exact at the working precision, instead of with one rounded floating-point operation per term. Each computed term rounds down, so their sum is a lower bound; each carries an error below 3 units of the last place, which gives an upper bound with a rigorous tail. The enclosure is about as wide as the floating-point one, the 12-attempt refinement loop and its working precisions are unchanged, and arguments that are not exact at the working precision still use the previous series. White-box tests check that the enclosure contains a much tighter one and that the final correctly rounded results and flags equal those of the previous series."
msgstr ""

