#: manual/performance/binary.md:292
msgid "The certified elementary functions memoize the constant enclosures they need (`ln 2`, `ln 10` and `pi`) per working precision, in small per-constant caches of six precisions up to 65,536 bits. A cached enclosure is the value a recomputation returns, so results never depend on cache state or call order. Before this, every `ln`, `log2`, `log10`, `sin`, `cos`, `tan` and `atan2` call re-ran an `ln 2` series or an `atan(1)` evaluation that cost as much as the function itself."
