#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:258
msgid "**The right operand is a pipeline.** Lift a plain value with `DecimalChecked::from_decimal(x, ctx)`, which rounds it into `ctx` first (a signaling NaN is quieted and raises `invalid_operation`); the operation then runs in the context of the left pipeline and rounds the result. The conditions of the right pipeline join the result, and its error stops the operation. To use the operand exactly (IEEE 754-2019 5.1: operands exact, one rounding), lift it in a context wide enough to hold it, such as `decimal128`; lifting at the precision of the left pipeline rounds twice. At three digits, `1.00 + 0.24500001` is `1.25` with a wide lift and `1.24` with a lift at three digits (the operand becomes `0.245` with `inexact`)."
