#: manual/tutorial/def.md:199
msgid "`Sign::Zero` does not mean \"the value is zero\". It is also returned for NaN by the scalar types. Test `@def.is_nan` first. `Interval` is not `Floating`: ask an interval `is_empty`, `is_common_interval` or `is_member`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/def.md:202
msgid "`Sign` cannot tell $-0$ from $+0$. Use the concrete package (`Binary::is_negative_zero`, `Decimal::is_sign_minus`) when the sign bit matters."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/def.md:205
msgid "`PartialOrder` is not an ordering you can sort with: `Unordered` breaks trichotomy. Use the total orders of the concrete packages (`Binary::total_order_compare`, `Decimal::total_order_compare`) for sorting."
