msgid "run the pinned corpora"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:31
msgid "Check one square root: $\\sqrt{2^{-1074} \\cdot 2^{52}} = 2^{-511}$ at 53 bits, rounding to nearest:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:48
msgid "Numbers are written as hexadecimal significand and binary exponent: `0x10000000000000p-1074` is $2^{52} \\cdot 2^{-1074}$."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:53
msgid "Elementary functions with flags"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:55
msgid "An elementary row names the function, the output precision and rounding, the operands, the expected result and three exception flags (inexact, invalid, division by zero). Unused operands are written `-` (second operand) and `0` (integer operand):"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:79
msgid "`ln(0) = -inf` raises division by zero and `sqrt(-1)` is an invalid operation returning NaN; both flags are part of the check."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:84
msgid "A `pow` row splits each number into coefficient, binary exponent and sign:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:99
msgid "The fields are: precision, rounding, input coefficient (hex digits), input exponent, input sign (`1` negative), integer exponent, expected coefficient, expected exponent, expected sign, inexact flag. Here `0x6c0p-9` is $1728/512 = 27/8$."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:104
msgid "Read a failure"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:125
msgid "The id is the operation (or `sqrt`/`pow`) and the line number."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:127
msgid "Parse errors"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:129
msgid "Every malformed line is reported with its line number, and no document is returned:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:148
msgid "**Corpora.** `just conformance run binary` executes the pinned MPFR `tests/data/sqrt` file and every `mpfrCorpora` entry of `testdata/binary/corpora.json` (the elementary matrix `mpfr-4.2.2-elementary.txt`, `mpfr-4.2.2-ln-wide.txt`, `mpfr-4.2.2-strtofr.txt` and `mpfr-4.2.2-decimal-output.txt`) together with TestFloat; see [verification](../../verification.md). The generators for the elementary and power data are `tools/generate_mpfr_elementary_oracle.c` and `tools/generate_mpfr_pow_oracle.c`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:156
msgid "**Which parser?** The CLI chooses the format of the first marker it finds, in the order `mpfr-decimal-random-v2`, `mpfr-random-v1`, `mpfr-strtofr-v1`, `mpfr-decimal-output-v1`, `mpfr-elementary-v1`, then the power format when the file contains `input_coefficient_hex`, and the square-root format otherwise. Put the marker in a comment line."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:164
msgid "**Elementary rows compare numbers, not encodings.** Any NaN matches an expected `nan`, and a zero must have the expected sign. Square-root and power rows compare the whole `Binary`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:167
msgid "**Square-root flags are not checked.** `sqrt` data rows compare only the value."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:169
msgid "**No exponent range.** Rows are executed in the context of the precision alone (`e_max` 1073741823, gradual underflow), and an elementary or power row that reports overflow or underflow fails."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:172
msgid "**Binary operations need a second operand.** An elementary `pow`, `powr`, `hypot`, `atan2` or `atan2pi` row with `-` as second operand is the parse diagnostic `invalid MPFR elementary field`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:175
msgid "**Inputs are read at 512 bits.** Power operands with longer significands are rounded before the function is evaluated; elementary operands are read at four bits per character of the token when that is more than 512."
msgstr ""

