#: manual/verification.md:940
msgid "Tininess detection for binary formats"
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:940
msgid "`BinaryContext` defaults to after rounding; before rounding is selectable and the TestFloat gate runs both. For decimal the standard requires before rounding and `decimal` always detects tininess before rounding; `DecimalContext` has no tininess option."
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:941
msgid "IEEE 754 §6.2"
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:941
msgid "Which NaN payload a NaN result carries"
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:941
msgid "`binary`: the sign of the selected NaN operand is kept, its payload keeps the low `p - 2` bits under a context, and a signaling NaN is quieted. `decimal`: the first NaN operand's sign and payload, cut to its low `p - 1` digits (the width of the interchange payload field; a `DecimalContext` is always clamped)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:942
msgid "IEEE 754 §9.7"
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:942
msgid "Admissible payloads of `setPayload`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:942
msgid "`decimal`: non-negative integers of at most `precision - 1` digits of the receiver; anything else gives `+0`. `binary` has no setPayload."
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:943
msgid "IEEE 754 §3.7"
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:943
msgid "Exponent range and precision of an extendable format"
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:943
msgid "`binary`: leading-bit exponents in `[2 - 2^30, 2^30 - 1]` (`e_min = 1 - e_max`), precision at most `2^28` bits. `decimal`: `e_min` and `e_max` within ±999,999,999, precision within `1..999,999,999`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:944
msgid "IEEE 754 §4.3"
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:944
msgid "Rounding directions beyond the five required"
msgstr ""

#: manual/verification.md:944
msgid "none in `binary` and `decimal` (the GDA modes `HalfDown`, `Up`, `ZeroFiveUp` are in `decimal_gda`)."
msgstr ""

